}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FyiurAmron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-19T08:00:49Z","updated_at":"2025-12-19T08:39:36Z","body":"@sockeye-d I mean, there is one valid case I can think of where changing resource type is indeed valid and expected, and that is going from `tres` to binary format. Currently it's allowed and works, and I think that case should stay. Apart from that one, I really can't think of any good reason for the user to change the extension, as it hides the file in UI and has all the expected problems (impossible to open/edit externally without further renaming etc.). Whether it should be allowed or not is debatable, but I think it's not arguable the window message should reflect this - maybe allow it but provide a yellow warning message about extension being changed and file potentially inaccessible? I'll throw that idea on the table.\r\n\r\nAlso, note that re \"completely disallowing changing the file extension\", it's actually already completely disallowed for non-imported files (`res`/`tres` etc.), simply because it always triggers an error when you do it. It's only possible (and was always only possible) for imported files, where I guess not many people will want to create a copy that simply doesn't work nor show anymore :)","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3673996403/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]